{"id":"word","name":"Word","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:word"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Word, The","text":"(Gr. Logos), one of the titles of our Lord, found only in the writings of John (John 1:1-14; 1 John 1:1; Rev. 19:13). As such, Christ is the revealer of God. His office is to make God known. “No man hath seen God at any time; the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him” (John 1:18). This title designates the divine nature of Christ. As the Word, he “was in the beginning” and “became flesh.” “The Word was with God ” and “was God,” and was the Creator of all things (comp. Ps. 33: 6; 107:20; 119:89; 147:18; Isa. 40:8)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3056","lemma":"λόγος","xlit":"lógos","gloss":"something said","kjv":"account, cause, communication, X concerning","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"G3962","lemma":"πατήρ","xlit":"patḗr","gloss":"a \"father\"","kjv":"father, parent","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["John.1.1","John.1.14","1John.5.7","Rev.19.13"],"related":[{"id":"titles-and-names-of-christ","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.022,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"character","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"conversation","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"epistles","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"gospel","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"hearers","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"instability","type":"lexical","strong":"G3056","why":"both lead with λόγος (G3056)"},{"id":"abba","type":"lexical","strong":"G3962","why":"both lead with πατήρ (G3962)"},{"id":"adoption","type":"lexical","strong":"G3962","why":"both lead with πατήρ (G3962)"},{"id":"apostles","type":"lexical","strong":"G3962","why":"both lead with πατήρ (G3962)"},{"id":"chr